  "targeting": [],
  "notes": [
    "demo-orders, demo-storefront and demo-profile were created before the scenario existed and their source was seeded with a single flag each. services.json declares demo-orders as consuming seven flags; its source referenced one. Seventeen flags therefore had targeting configured and were being evaluated zero times.",
    "Widening source is what starts their evaluation history. Targeting without a caller accumulates nothing, and evaluation history is real elapsed time, so every hour a flag spends unreferenced is baseline that cannot be recovered.",
    "Deployment widens from 12 to 16 evaluators: all seven Node services on both critical environments, plus demo-orders retaining Test and Dev for its bounded probe. Connections are no longer the constraint — measured duty cycle is 0.27 per cent, so sixteen batch evaluators cost far less than one sustained connection.",
    "Expected effect: flags with a deployed caller rise from 7 to 19. The five without one are demo-retired-banner and the three never-started flags, all deliberately silent, plus demo-sms-notifications whose only consumer is the TypeScript service that does not exist yet."
  ]
